Subject: [PATCH] C13, patch 3 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M19; main's
 fourth folder, item 4): THE TOPIC SWEEP PRINTS THE LEDGER'S ROW OF A WALL
 BEFORE ITS OWN LIST

Main asks that scripts/checks/topic_sweep.py print the ledger's row of any wall whose words the expression
matches, before its own list: the first step of main's new rule, a question of a known shape met with its
history first.

WHAT IS BUILT.
  - The sweep reads the generated page of the ledger of walls and nothing else, so that what it prints is
    what the page says. For each wall whose name or one of whose words the expression matches (the
    expression as the sweep expands it by its aliases), it prints one line before the first arc: the wall,
    its count of arcs, where it was first met, its five outcomes, and the page's section.
  - A sweep on a checkout without the page says so on one line and goes on.
  - The sweep's VERDICT line is not changed, so nothing that reads it is changed.
  - The sweep's self-test gains two planted walls, a hit by a word, a hit by a name, and a planted absence.

THE WORDS OF A WALL ARE THE BUILDER'S READING, AND MAIN'S TO CHANGE. B1905's rows give each wall a name and
no words. Each wall's words are its name and the words of B1905's own sweep (its "Seen first"), each put
under the wall it names, with a few of the same kind; the eighth wall, "other", has its name alone. They
are declared beside the ledger's generator and printed on the ledger's page in a last table, so the page
and the sweep cannot disagree about them.

THE TEST, tests/test_topic_sweep_prints_the_wall.py, six tests. What the sweep reads from the page is what
the generator put there, words included; a sweep on a word of the first wall prints that wall's row and
prints it before the first arc, and the verdict line is the last line as before; a sweep by a wall's name
and by another wall's word; a sweep that matches no wall prints none; a checkout without the page; the page
with one count planted is read as planted (the sweep reads the page; the ledger's own lock is what refuses
such a page), and its twin, the page copied as it is, reads the same. On the commit before this patch four
of the six fail and two pass: the absence and the self-test.

Every gate passes but the count of landings. The sweep's three older test files, the ledger's lock and the
lock of B1905: 35 passed. Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote it.
